{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JER",
  "chapter": 48,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JER.48.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Against Moab thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Woe to Nebo! for it is laid waste: Kiriathaim is confounded ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " taken: Misgab is confounded and dismayed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no more praise of Moab: in Heshbon they have devised evil against it; come, and let us cut it off from ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "being",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a nation. Also thou shalt be cut down, O Madmen; the sword shall pursue thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A voice of crying ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from Horonaim, devastation and great destruction.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moab is destroyed; her little ones have caused a cry to be heard.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For in the ascent of Luhith continual weeping shall go up; for in the descent of Horonaim the enemies have heard a cry of destruction.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Flee, save your lives, and be like the heath in the wilderness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For because thou hast trusted in thy works and in thy treasures, thou also shalt be taken: and Chemosh shall go forth into captivity ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his priests and his princes together.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the spoiler shall come upon every city, and no city shall escape: the valley also shall perish, and the plain shall be destroyed, as the LORD hath spoken.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Give wings to Moab, that it may flee and get away: for its cities shall be desolate, without any to dwell in them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Cursed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that doeth the work of the LORD deceitfully, and cursed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that keepeth back his sword from blood.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moab hath been at ease from his youth, and he hath settled on his lees, and hath not been emptied from vessel to vessel, neither hath he gone into captivity: therefore his taste remained in him, and his scent is not changed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore, behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that I will send to him wanderers that shall cause him to wander, and shall empty his vessels, and break their bottles.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Moab shall be ashamed of Chemosh, as the house of Israel was ashamed of Beth-el their confidence.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How say ye, We ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mighty and strong men for the war?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moab is laid waste, and gone up ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "out of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " her cities, and his chosen young men are gone down to the slaughter, saith the king, whose name ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD of hosts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The calamity of Moab ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " near to come, and his affliction hasteth fast.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All ye that are about him bemoan him; and all ye that know his name, say, How is the strong staff broken, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the beautiful rod!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou daughter that dost inhabit Dibon, come down from ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thy",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " glory, and sit in thirst; for the spoiler of Moab shall come upon thee, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he shall destroy thy strong holds.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O inhabitant of Aroer, stand by the way, and espy; ask him that fleeth, and her that escapeth, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " say, What is done?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moab is confounded; for it is broken down: howl and cry; tell ye it in Arnon, that Moab is laid waste.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And judgment is come upon the plain country; upon Holon, and upon Jahazah, and upon Mephaath,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And upon Dibon, and upon Nebo, and upon Beth-diblathaim,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And upon Kiriathaim, and upon Beth-gamul, and upon Beth-meon,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And upon Kerioth, and upon Bozrah, and upon all the cities of the land of Moab, far or near.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The horn of Moab is cut off, and his arm is broken, saith the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Make ye him drunken; for he magnified ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "himself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " against the LORD: Moab also shall wallow in his vomit, and he also shall be in derision.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For was not Israel a derision to thee? was he found among thieves? for since thou hast spoken of him, thou hast leaped for joy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O ye that dwell in Moab, leave the cities, and dwell in the rock, and be like the dove ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " maketh her nest in the sides of the hole's mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We have heard the pride of Moab, (he is exceeding proud) his loftiness, and his arrogance, and his pride, and the haughtiness of his heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I know his wrath, saith the LORD; but ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it shall",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " so; his lies shall not so effect ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore will I howl for Moab, and I will cry out for all Moab; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my heart",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall mourn for the men of Kirheres.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O vine of Sibmah, I will weep for thee with the weeping of Jazer: thy plants have gone over the sea, they reach ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the sea of Jazer: the spoiler hath fallen upon thy summer fruits and upon thy vintage.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And joy and gladness is taken from the plentiful field, and from the land of Moab; and I have caused wine to fail from the wine-presses: none shall tread with shouting; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shouting ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no shouting.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "From the cry of Heshbon ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to Elealeh, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to Jahaz, have they uttered their voice, from Zoar ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to Horonaim, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a heifer of three years old: for the waters also of Nimrim shall be desolate.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moreover I will cause to cease in Moab, saith the LORD, him that offereth in the high places, and him that burneth incense to his gods.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore my heart shall sound for Moab like pipes, and my heart shall sound like pipes for the men of Kirheres: because the riches ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he hath gotten have perished.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For every head ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bald, and every beard clipped: upon all the hands ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cuttings, and upon the loins sackcloth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " lamentation generally upon all the house-tops of Moab, and in its streets: for I have broken Moab like a vessel in which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no pleasure, saith the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They shall howl, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "saying",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", How is it broken down! how hath Moab turned the back with shame! so shall Moab be a derision and a dismaying to all them about him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thus saith the LORD; Behold, he shall fly as an eagle, and shall spread his wings over Moab.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Kerioth is taken, and the strong holds are surprised, and the mighty men's hearts in Moab at that day shall be as the heart of a woman in her pangs.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Moab shall be destroyed from ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "being",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a people, because he hath magnified ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "himself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " against the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.43",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.43",
      "verse": 43,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fear, and the pit, and the snare, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon thee, O inhabitant of Moab, saith the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.44",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.44",
      "verse": 44,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that fleeth from the fear, shall fall into the pit; and he that getteth out of the pit, shall be taken in the snare: for I will bring upon it, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon Moab, the year of their visitation, saith the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.45",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.45",
      "verse": 45,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They that fled stood under the shade of Heshbon because of the force: but a fire shall come out of Heshbon, and a flame from the midst of Sihon, and shall devour the corner of Moab, and the crown of the head of the tumultuous ones.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.46",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.46",
      "verse": 46,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Woe be to thee, O Moab! the people of Chemosh perisheth: for thy sons are taken captives, and thy daughters captives.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.48.47",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.48.47",
      "verse": 47,
      "spans": [
        {
